sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-agential-02> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Because metazoan cells are agential (they retain adaptive behaviours from unicellular ancestors), what evolution mainly searches is not the enormous space of all possible local rules but the space of behaviour-shaping signals by which cells hack each other's functionality, and the collective intelligence of cell swarms strongly affects the rate and course of evolution.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Evolution searches the space of behaviour-shaping signals rather than local rules";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Darwin's agential materials: evolutionary implications of multiscale competency in developmental biology”, Cellular and molecular life sciences : CMLS (2023), doi:10.1007/s00018-023-04790-z; section “From genotype to phenotype in development: implications of an indirect pathway”. Scope: Evolution of metazoan anatomy"
}
